 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:06.245224Z",
 "text": "Yes, this clause is enforceable. Under subsection 26(1)(b) of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord is expressly permitted to enter a rental unit at any time without written notice if the tenant consents to the entry at the time of entry. Because the clause requires the tenant's agreement \"at that time\" (rather than purporting to grant blanket advance consent in the lease itself), it aligns with the Act and is valid.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 26",
